PROBLEMS ENCOUNTERED AND FIXED (also affecting Login/Register)
------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Password "Show" toggle button rendered oversized and overlapping
   the Login button. Root cause: a CSS rule intended only for the
   submit button (width: 100%, teal background) was written generically
   as ".auth-form button", so it applied to every button in the form,
   including the toggle.
   Fix: scoped that rule specifically to button[type="submit"].

2. Typed text in the Email/Password fields was invisible on some
   screens. Root cause: index.css still contained the original Vite
   template's demo styling, including a @media (prefers-color-scheme:
   dark) block that overrode text color based on the visitor's system/
   browser theme - a leftover from Day 11 that was never fully cleaned
   out.
   Fix: replaced index.css with a minimal reset, and added an explicit
   color rule for inputs/selects/textareas/buttons in App.css so form
   text is never affected by the visitor's system theme.

